imports them rather than keeping its own copies: auditing a plan therefore
exercises the same code the sweep will run. On top of that it provides
:func:`test_partitions`, which builds a whole sweep of partitions up front,
proves that no patient ever crosses a split boundary, and writes a JSON
description plus a Plotly HTML report.

The patient-level guarantee matters most on trace-level data, where a patient
contributes one row per valid ``device_channel`` instead of a single clustered
row. Splitting on rows there would scatter one patient's traces across train
